# Real lines from the same spike capture (publish-trimmed.log) as
# trim-warnings-sample.log, but from LhmDump's OWN Program.cs (the spike's
# diagnostic dump code, never part of oma-service) — kept separate to prove
# scripts/check-trim-warnings.ps1 correctly fails on both of these real shapes:
#
# 1. A Roslyn compile-time trim-analyzer warning with NO origin member printed
#    at all (just "warning ILxxxx: <prose message>"), unlike the ILLink
#    publish-time warning for the same call site. The parser must not guess an
#    origin here: this counts as unparseable and fails closed (requirement 2).
# 2. A path-prefixed "Trim analysis warning" WITH an origin the parser CAN
#    extract (Program.Main(String[])), but that origin is not on
#    ../../service/trim-allowlist.txt — a normal "unlisted" failure, proving a
#    real, well-formed origin still isn't waved through just because it parses.
#
# Expected: scripts/check-trim-warnings.ps1 -ParseOnly -InputLog <this file>
# exits 1 on both lines.
